            "anno" : "Retinoblastoma protein binding E1A, 12S mRNA product (243R in HAdV-5)",
            "comment" : "12S product (distal 5' splice site); lacks the internal 46-aa segment of the 289R protein (PMID 2968533). Junctions come from the literature: HAdV-5 13S 560..1112,1229.. / 12S 560..974,1229.. (PMID 2958276; verified on AC_000008); HAdV-2 559..1111/973,1226.. (PMID 33239457); HAdV-4 576..1140/1047,1233.. (PMID 2947381, reconstructed from the stated 257/226 aa); BAdV-3 606..1215,1323.. (13S only; the authors' own deposit AF030154, PMID 9918888). Extended to other genomes by aligning the donor and acceptor regions to the nearest anchor (two passes, multiple and pairwise; a genome is kept only where the passes agree); start = the in-frame ATG closest to the protein-aligned start; GT/GC..AG required unless the flanks are conserved in context (>=0.8). The 12S product takes the 13S acceptor (shared exon 2, PMID 15068396) and must reproduce the 13S C-terminus exactly. Every distinct product was translated and aligned with the anchor products: exon 2 must align in frame, the product must end in the E1A exon-2 CtBP motif (PxDLS and variants) or match an anchor's own end (the BAdV-3 211R form lacks it), and products with ambiguity codes were removed. References built from deposits were NOT used: 16/26 HAdV-C 12S deposits gave the right protein with the junction 3 nt early (AG..AA). Mastadenovirus: anchors HAdV-2/4/5 cover species C and E directly; other species and animal lineages are site-alignment extensions, each checked as above. 735 unique references, products 215-246 aa. min_len = 0.95 x the shortest reference product.",
